{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37496-alternate-identity-as-new-cover","id":37496,"title":"Alternate Identity AS new Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-26T14:02:49-08:00","id":37496,"title":"Alternate Identity AS new Cover","content":"As the title, if a Demon buy the Merit for a Cover... later, can &quot;cash&quot; the new identity as Cover for him/her self?<br /> Or : merge the new (or old?) identity with his actual Cover?<br /> What do you think about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T14:11:07-08:00","id":37500,"title":"","content":"No. Alternate Identity is purchased as an asset for a Cover identity, it's not a full identity in itself. As with mortals, it just represents a false paper trail and a reputation having forged a new persona. It has no metaphysical weight, no associated infrastructure, actual history or real associations beyond what the actual Cover identity has. A Cover identity is an entire artificial personhood; Alternate Identity is just lies a person tells.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: That said, an Alternate Identity that lays claim to aspects possessed by other people could be actualized by creating a patchwork Cover. It would be tricky work, since you'd have to find people with pieces of lives that match the lies you've told, but yield a Cover with a better girded history and access to assets already established by the Alternate Identity. You'd still need to work with the raw materials of human lives, though, to build the supernatural aspects of the Cover.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;merging an Alternate Identity with your Cover,&quot; that's the default state of the Merit in Demon; an Alternate Identity provides your Cover identity with a double life. That Cover identity </i>is<i> both people.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-26-2013, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T14:38:09-08:00","id":37508,"title":"","content":"I feel like I'm going to use Breaking Bad as an example a lot when discussing D:tD...<br /> A Demon, let's call him Asmodeus, has Walter White as one of his Covers: a chemistry teacher with lung cancer and a family.<br /> Walter White has the Alternate Identity of Heisenberg; while he's a drug lord instead of a teacher, Heisenberg's still supposed to be a chemistry pro, still has lung cancer, and still has a family, he might just want to hide it all for his own safety.<br /> When you investigate Walter White thoroughly, it should be fairly easy to figure out he's Heisenberg, or vice versa. Harm one, and you harm the other in exactly the same way; shatter one as a Cover, and they both crumble down. Walter White and Heisenberg mostly share the same characteristics. If one is witnessed doing something that only the other would do, that would be more likely to damage the Alternate Identity than the single Cover they both form.<br /> It should be, however, much more difficult to figure out that Walter and/or Heisenberg are actually Asmodeus, who doesn't have lungs, can't have cancer, and has no real family to speak of; he might be attached to them, but that's no guarantee. When you investigate Walter/Heisenberg, there's no guarantee you'll find Asmodeus, especially when you're just a mere mortal. When you destroy Walter and Heisenberg as Covers, Asmodeus still lives and exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T07:22:43-08:00","id":37843,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T17:45:03-08:00","id":38507,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.. i wonder if establishing an alternate identity would damage your cover unless you deliberately lie within lies. If the demon ACTS like a wholly different identity, itd damage his cover. But if he acts like an actor pretending to be someone else (rather than acting like he isnt his cover, he is acting like his cover is acting like hes someone else) it might not. Either way.. i think alternate identities of the mortal sort wouldve been a hot topic in the demon book if it werent hard to do. Id be relatively stern when it came to it, as it buffers the cover. Id definately call compromise rolls if the demon was neglecting his cover in order to create its alternate identity. But if he succeeded, itd be like cover body armor for compromise rolls in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T17:57:16-08:00","id":38512,"title":"","content":"I feel as though this is fallow ground for an Interlock or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T18:26:18-08:00","id":38532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37496-alternate-identity-as-new-cover?p=38512#post38512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though this is fallow ground for an Interlock or two.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps an interlock that temporary empowers a second identity into a full cover, absorbing compromise rolls, can be burned to go loud, etc. Probably damages or destroys the alternate identity though, making this power a very cool climax if investigators have traced the demon's false identity close enough to him to endanger is real cover. He then &quot;burns&quot; his alternate identity for a scene of ass kicking compromise free activities. Id say that using this to go loud should cause a compromise roll (as going loud is a hypercharged and highly noticeable event regardless of double covers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T18:53:56-08:00","id":38537,"title":"","content":"Or possibly using an Alternate Identity as the rigging for a patchwork Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:29:46-08:00","id":38783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37496-alternate-identity-as-new-cover?p=38507#post38507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.. i wonder if establishing an alternate identity would damage your cover unless you deliberately lie within lies. If the demon ACTS like a wholly different identity, itd damage his cover. But if he acts like an actor pretending to be someone else (rather than acting like he isnt his cover, he is acting like his cover is acting like hes someone else) it might not. Either way.. i think alternate identities of the mortal sort wouldve been a hot topic in the demon book if it werent hard to do. Id be relatively stern when it came to it, as it buffers the cover. Id definately call compromise rolls if the demon was neglecting his cover in order to create its alternate identity. But if he succeeded, itd be like cover body armor for compromise rolls in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div> The term for what you're describing here is APC, or Actor Portraying Character, and it is something actors frequently do, especially in experimental theater. You also see it a lot in film with actors who have these big personas that come through in almost every character they play. Johnny Depp, for example, rarely ever just plays a character any more, he plays &quot;Johnny Depp As [character]&quot; but of course, &quot;Johnny Depp As&quot; is himself a film persona, and not how Johnny probably behaves in everyday life. As it's something human actors can learn to do with the right training, I would say Demons (who have perfect control over what emotions they display) could easily just do an APC alternate identity second-nature, and would not require compromise rolls or any other sort of special work besides jugs buying alternate identity. In fact, I imagine they would have a much easier time at it than humans, being very used to living double lives and hiding lies with other lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}